PLACEHOLDER — replace with a real 128x128 PNG before publishing.

The VS Code Marketplace requires `icon.png` to be a 128×128 raster
PNG. We ship an SVG (media/tars-icon.svg) for the Activity Bar but
the Marketplace listing image must be PNG.

How to produce the real binary
------------------------------

  cd vscode-extension
  # If you have rsvg-convert (librsvg) installed:
  rsvg-convert -w 128 -h 128 media/tars-icon.svg -o icon.png

  # Or with ImageMagick:
  magick convert -background none -resize 128x128 \
      media/tars-icon.svg icon.png

  # Or open media/tars-icon.svg in Figma / Sketch / Affinity
  # and export at 128x128 @ 1x as PNG, save as icon.png at the
  # extension root.

`scripts/PUBLISH-EXTENSION.command` will refuse to publish while
this file is still text (it sniffs the PNG magic bytes).
